Convert a JSON text into a JavaScript object.

Convert a JSON text into a JavaScript array.

JSON.parse()can parse any valid JSON value.

A common use of JSON is to exchange data to/from a web server.

When receiving data from a web server, thedata is a string:

UseJSON.parse()to convert text string into aJavaScript object:

Use data from the the object on your page:

Theoptionalreviver argument is acallback functionused to transform the parsed data.

It accepts two arguments: a propertykeyand itsvalue.

Thereturn valuereplaces the original value:

JSON does not supportDate objects, so they are serialized as strings.
A reviver can be used to convert date strings back into actual JavaScript Date instances upon parsing:

If the JSON text isnot valid, JSON.parse() throws aSyntaxError.

Usetry...catchto handle invalid JSON.

JSON.parse()expects JSON text, not a JavaScript object.

After JSON has been parsed, the result is already a JavaScript value.

### Code Snippets

```
JSON.parse(text, reviver)

---

const text = '{"name":"John","age":30,"city":"New York"}';
const person = JSON.parse(text);
let name= person.name;

